## 2. Findings

| # | Finding | Severity | Host | Port | Evidence | Recommendation |
|---|---------|----------|------|------|----------|----------------|
| 1 | Outdated Apache HTTP server (2.4.25) | High | target-server | 80 | `nmap -sV` / `curl -I` Server header | Upgrade Apache to a supported release; hide the version banner (`ServerTokens Prod`). |
| 2 | DVWA default credentials (admin/password) | Critical | target-server | 80 | Successful login at http://10.20.40.10/login.php | Remove default accounts; enforce strong, unique passwords. |
| 3 | SQL Injection in DVWA sqli module | Critical | target-server | 80 | UNION payload returns the `dvwa` database and `users` table | Use parameterised queries / prepared statements; validate input. |
| 4 | phpMyAdmin exposed on the network | High | target-server | 8080 | HTTP 200 at http://10.20.40.10:8080/ | Restrict admin panels to management networks; require authentication. |
| 5 | SSH weak credentials (labuser/labuser) | Critical | target-server | 22 | `ssh labuser@10.20.40.10` with password `labuser` | Enforce strong passwords / key-based auth; disable password login. |
| 6 | MariaDB exposed to the network | Medium | target-server | 3306 | `nmap -sV -p 3306` returns MariaDB 10.11 | Bind the database to localhost / internal VLAN only; firewall port 3306. |

